WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.520
I normally test the
latest beauty releases,

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.920
but today I'm testing out
the most-hyped products

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.870
from the early 2000s.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.670
Let's start with some face products.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.960
You know I had to include

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.600
the Maybelline Dream
Matte mousse foundation.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.600
I feel like this was a lot
of people's first foundation,

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.100
mine included.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.250
The formula is like this chunky mousse

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.760
with a bunch of little beads
that mattify the foundation.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.000
I had to apply it with my
fingers at first, of course.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.400
This foundation is just really odd to me.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.870
It doesn't look like skin,

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:33.129
it doesn't look even, it's kind of drying,

00:00:33.129 --> 00:00:36.870
and I can literally see the
color changing before my eyes.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.120
I looked in the mirror, and
I was straight-up orange,

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.520
which I guess is fitting for this era.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.920
Loose-powder mineral
makeup was such a big thing

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.090
in the 2000s.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:48.180
I've never tried this bareMinerals
powder foundation before,

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.060
but I was actually pleasantly surprised.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.580
I don't think it's as
buildable as it claims to be.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.770
I feel like wearing it sheer looks better

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.600
than when you keep layering it.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.730
But I liked how this looked on my skin.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:00.930
It wasn't too drying,

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.840
but I did need a setting spray
to kind of melt it all in.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.790
It feels weightless, which I really liked,

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:08.460
and everything I put on
top of this looked nice.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.250
This also has SPF in
it, and it's talc-free.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.720
This one triggered me

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.750
because I remember trying to
hide my acne with this stuff.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.900
This is the Maybelline Cover
Stick corrector concealer.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.820
It's a very thick formula,

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.530
it doesn't spread super easily,

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:25.050
and I can feel it on my skin.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.383
It actually did a decent job

00:01:26.383 --> 00:01:28.470
of covering everything
I needed it to cover,

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:30.300
but concealer formulas have just gotten

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.860
so much better than this.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.600
Plus, the shade range is abysmal.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.280
This one can stay in the past.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.430
Bronzer usage was at an
all-time high in the 2000s,

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.860
and this one was always a popular choice.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.600
This is the Nars Laguna bronzer.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:45.300
It's a bronzer with a bunch
of gold shimmer in it.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.270
Surprisingly, this looked
pretty smooth on the face,

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.150
even on top of that
Maybelline mousse foundation.

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.923
I thought that and the shimmer in it

00:01:52.923 --> 00:01:55.500
would emphasize all of my
texture, but it didn't.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.260
It also didn't look orange,
which I was also nervous about.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:01.830
I also tried the classic
Benefit Cosmetics Hoola bronzer.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.200
This one also applies very smoothly.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.690
It has no shimmer in it, which I prefer.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:09.540
I believe back then, Benefit
only had this one shade,

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:11.430
which was a little light for me.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.980
The shade range still
hasn't expanded very much,

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.840
but this formula has held up.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.840
This is the iconic Nars
blush in the shade Orgasm.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:19.920
It's a peachy pink

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.200
with a ridiculous amount
of gold shimmer in it.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.520
It claims to be buildable,

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.750
but the more I layered this

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.840
for that very 2000s pink-blush look,

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.800
the more textured my skin looked.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.650
Like, this highlighted everything.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.260
It's weird because I applied
a lot of the bronzer too,

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.910
which also has shimmer in it,

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:37.380
and it didn't look like this.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.150
This blush is just not for me.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:42.480
The Urban Decay Primer Potion
is a tried-and-true favorite.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.890
The formula is thinner

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.020
than other eyeshadow bases I've tried.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.085
I used a super-cheap CoverGirl
eyeshadow on top of this,

00:02:49.085 --> 00:02:51.630
and I feel like it actually
made it look way better.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.550
It makes it easy to blend out shadow.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.650
I feel like it intensifies the color.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:56.970
This is way overpriced,

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.310
but I think this is a
solid eyeshadow primer.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:02.160
I saw so many of these
CoverGirl Eye Enhancers

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.960
in my research for this video.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.180
They are just as chalky as they look.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:08.550
The colors I chose may be the reason why,

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.560
but I can't talk about 2000s makeup

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.170
without some frosty blue
and white eyeshadow.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.490
I think if I hadn't used them

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.680
on top of that Urban Decay Primer Potion,

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.600
they just would have not shown up.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.030
Look at these swatches
on the back of my hand.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:22.530
Just awful.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:25.020
I will say that these
little sponge applicators

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.520
that I used to always throw away

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.830
actually apply the eyeshadow pretty well.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:31.440
Now, these I still use all the time.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.840
These are the Nyx jumbo eye pencils.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.490
You can use them for so much.

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:39.300
As an eyeshadow, as a base
for eyeshadow, as an eyeliner.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.520
These got a new life because of TikTok.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:42.540
People were using them

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:44.760
to highlight certain areas of the face.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:48.000
The formula is just super
creamy and easy to work with.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.670
It is kind of a pain to
sharpen when you need to,

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:53.040
but I like the formula,
so I just deal with it.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.590
I also still use and
really like this product.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:58.710
This is the Urban Decay
Heavy Metal glitter eyeliner.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:01.470
This does dry down quickly,
so you want to work fast,

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:04.260
but I think it adds the
prettiest sparkle to the eyes.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:07.020
It's an easy way to use
glitter without any mess.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.510
I will say this doesn't
layer very well, though.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:11.880
It can get flaky if you layer it too much.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.860
This is the MAC Smolder eyeliner.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.248
I had to try this
specific eyeliner because

00:04:16.248 --> 00:04:19.448
Avril Lavigne said she used
to use this one all the time.

00:04:19.448 --> 00:04:21.180
I don't typically like wooden eyeliners,

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.010
but this one applied really well.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.660
I have very sensitive eyes,

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.760
so my waterline gets super watery

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.230
when I try to apply eyeliner,

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.750
but the pigment actually
stuck with this one.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.540
I actually used to love the
Maybelline Great Lash mascara.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.850
I think the formula is pretty good.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:37.380
It doesn't give a ton of length,

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.290
but it gives a nice amount of
volume without getting clumpy.

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:42.330
I honestly think if it
had a different brush,

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:43.620
I'd like it more.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.840
In a sea of drugstore mascaras,

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.640
I don't think I'd go back to this one,

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.757
but I appreciate it for what it is.

00:04:49.757 --> 00:04:53.100
DuWop Lip Venom is like
the OG lip plumper.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.870
The tingle with this is pretty strong,

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:57.450
so if you hate that
feeling, I would avoid this.

00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:00.390
It has this really nice cinnamony scent,

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:02.400
and it gives a really nice shine.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.720
I like that it's a clear shade

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.850
that you can put on top of anything.

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:08.280
I noticed the plumping more on my top lip,

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.840
but it definitely plumps.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:13.050
And I noticed that it also made
my lips look a bit smoother.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:16.500
MAC lipsticks were so
popular in the 2000s.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.410
Myth was, like, the concealer lip shade.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:20.820
It's this super-pale nude

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.640
that looks ridiculous on
me without a lip liner.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:26.190
And Snob is this pale pastel-pink color

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:28.170
that reminds me of Nicki Minaj.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:29.730
Also looks awful on me.

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:31.860
Aside from the questionable color choices,

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:34.320
the MAC satin lipstick
formula still holds up.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:35.910
It's comfortable on the lips,

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.890
and the formula is pretty buildable.

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:40.350
Also, the vanilla scent of MAC lipsticks

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:41.850
always takes me back.

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:44.160
This is the MAC lip liner in Spice.

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:45.600
I loved this.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:48.240
This lip liner formula
applies really smoothly.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.710
It doesn't dry down too quickly,

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:51.450
so you have time to blend.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.300
I tried to do a
super-defined-lip-liner look

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:56.460
with that Myth lipstick,
and I actually loved it.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.380
I'm definitely going to keep using this.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:01.560
I've waited my whole life
to try the MAC Lipglass.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.570
This is very thick, I will say.

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:06.000
I personally love the
feeling of a thick gloss.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.440
I love how cushiony it is,

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:09.810
but you definitely feel this on the lips.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:11.550
I know why they call it Lipglass,

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.340
because the shine this gives is unreal.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.600
I'm in love with this.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.550
I also tried a Lancôme Juicy Tube,

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:21.240
which is like the archnemesis
to the MAC Lipglass.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.290
I picked this color

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:23.610
because it looks just like the one

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.260
that Gretchen Wieners uses.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.360
It has a scent I really dislike.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.880
It's kind of floral-perfume-y.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:31.800
The actual formula is nice.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.390
It's thinner than the Lipglass

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.460
but still really shiny and pretty.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.440
I don't think this is
anything that special.

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:40.650
The Nars lip gloss in Turkish
Delight feels very 2000s.

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.290
It's this pale, milky pink color.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.780
I think this used to be Kim
Kardashian's favorite gloss,

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:47.490
which, I don't know why.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.310
This formula is kind of oily and thin.

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:52.230
I don't know if it used
to be a different formula,

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:54.180
but it's not very good now.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.970
This color also settles into
the wrinkles on my lips,

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.130
so it's just not super flattering.

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:01.530
I could not do a 2000s makeup video

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:04.140
without mentioning Lip
Smacker's lip glosses.

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:06.327
They're more like a lip gloss for kids.

00:07:06.327 --> 00:07:07.590
Like, my mom bought me these

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:09.930
before I was allowed to wear any makeup.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.900
They're not actually a
good lip-gloss formula.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:14.940
They feel like chicken grease on the lips,

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:15.930
but you know what?

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:19.440
They still smell and taste
just as good as you remember.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:22.020
I would never buy these as
a serious lip-gloss option,

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.423
but using them again has
brought me so much joy.

